":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the streak-counter read-modify-write is serialized against concurrent reclaim-gate processes (e.g. flock on the state dir, or an explicit statement that the timer/throttle guarantees single-flight), not only that the write is atomic via mv.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The reclaim gate runs as a SEPARATE autodeploy.sh process on every ~2-min timer tick'","'written via write-tmp-then-mv (atomic rename, so a torn write is never observed)' — addresses torn write but not the check-then-act read-modify-write across processes","'throttled for PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL (600s)' — a throttle is not a mutual-exclusion lock; the plan does not state the counter update is serialized against a concurrent gate process"],"finding":"The persisted streak counter's read-modify-write is not shown to be atomic across concurrent reclaim-gate invocations. The plan specifies atomic write (write-tmp-then-mv, so a torn write is never observed) but a mv only makes the WRITE atomic — it does not serialize the read-then-increment-then-write sequence. If two reclaim-gate processes run in the same window (the throttle is time-based, not a lock), both read the same value N, both write N+1, and one increment is lost, delaying the persistence marker.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f998af43044595155","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Persistence and configurability of the streak counter'","norm_id":"n0ad21ffb35d7a8c7","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two timer ticks (or a manual invocation overlapping a scheduled one) enter the reclaim path close together; both read streak=2, both write 3, so a persistent-pressure sequence that should have reached PRESSURE_STREAK_ALARM=3 undercounts and the ineffective-reclaim marker is delayed or never emitted."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Guard the reclaim-gate critical section (read counter -> reclaim -> recompute -> write counter) with a flock on a lockfile under $STATE_DIR so overlapping timer ticks cannot both increment from a stale read; document that the throttle alone does not provide mutual exclusion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"78afed5a84288d7a","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["2bca834e0a4bae14",7808],"description_boxes":["399141be1d30ac26",0],"file_impact":["2cb64d050e22aa67",6],"ticket_id":["edc0f56c5de62cc6",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a loc